Patch: 007-code-mode-nested
Reason: a host tool a code-mode model's script calls arrives as a nested call under an id of Codex's own (exec-<uuid>) that no rollout line carries, and nothing on the app-server's stream names the exec it belongs to, so a never tool's barrier waited for a line that never comes and the call was declined for good; it is tied to the one live script (the exec's line in the log, kept until an output says it finished, a yielded script's cell until the wait that finishes it, and the exec the proxy's latest answer carried) and is held until that exec's line is in the log, and declined while two scripts are live
Upstream: ours
Pins: code mode: an exec that calls a never host tool runs it exactly once
Pins: code mode: two nested calls of one exec (a Promise.all) each pass the barrier once, under the one exec, and run once
Pins: code mode: a never tool called after its exec yielded runs once, under the cell that is still running
Pins: code mode: a model that writes a new exec while a cell still runs: a never tool its new script calls is declined, not run
